# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# Node
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
release
# Anchored and directory-only: the old unanchored `release-*` matched at any
# depth and silently swallowed scripts/release-sweep.mjs — the release gate
# `npm run sweep` runs — so it lived on one machine and was missing from every
# clone. Build output only from here on.
/release-*/
# Generated by scripts/build-release-notes.mjs; CI writes it before the release
# step reads it, so it is an artifact rather than a source file.
/RELEASE_NOTES.md
/RigMatch.AI-main/
*.local

# Rust / Tauri build artifacts (can be several GB — never commit)
rigmatch-chat/src-tauri/target/
rigmatch-chat/src-tauri/gen/

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# OS
Thumbs.db

# Generated at release time from src/data/releaseNotes.ts (CHANGELOG.md is committed).
RELEASE_NOTES.md

# Internal / not for publishing
SESSION_NOTES.md
review-ai-handoff/
design/

# Built, not authored. CI runs `tauri build` and copies its own companion here
# on every run, so a committed binary is never the one that ships — it was only
# ever overwritten. Seventeen versions of it had reached 248 MB of history, and
# because it sat in every checkout, the Linux and macOS packages picked it up
# and shipped a Windows .exe they could never execute.
#
# Local builds still need it: `npm run prepare:companions` copies it from
# rigmatch-chat/src-tauri/target/release, and says so if you have not built it.
companions/
